d hooks capabilities\n\n5. **v2.1.162 - Enhanced Agent CLI & Tool Specifications**\n   - **Update Type:** Feature\n   - **Date:** 2026-06-03\n   - **URL:** https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code/releases/tag/v2.1.162\n   - **Description:** Enhanced `claude agents --json` with waitingFor field, improved tool specification for Grep/Glob on native builds, added `/effort` persistence confirmation, and enhanced slash command autocomplete behavior\n\n6. **v2.1.161 - OpenTelemetry Integration & Enhanced MCP Management**\n   - **Update Type:** Feature\n   - **Date:** 2026-06-02\n   - **URL:** https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code/releases/tag/v2.1.161\n   - **Description:** OpenTelemetry integration with custom label support, improved `claude agents` UI with progress indicators, enhanced `/mcp` connector management with unused connector collapsing, and improved parallel tool call error handling\n\n7. **v2.1.160 - Safety Prompts for Config File Writes**\n   - **Update Type:** Feature\n   - **Date:** 2026-06-02\n   - **URL:** https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code/releases/tag/v2.1.160\n   - **Description:** Added safety prompts before writing to shell startup files and git config, enhanced acceptEdits mode to prompt before build-tool config writes, and improved Edit tool behavior after grep operations\n\n### **Aider**\n**No updates found in the May 23 - June 6, 2026 timeframe:**\n- Latest release was v0.86.0 on 2025-08-09, which is outside the requested time window\n\n### **Continue.dev**\n**No updates found in the May 23 - June 6, 2026 timeframe:**\n- Latest releases were from March 2026 (v1.3.38-vscode on 2026-03-27), which are outside the requested time window\n\n### **Cursor, GitHub Copilot, Windsurf, Devin, Codex CLI, Gemini CLI**\n**No updates found in the May 23 - June 6, 2026 timeframe:**\n- Unable to access recent releases via GitHub API for these tools\n- No local data available for these specific tools in the requested timeframe\n\n### **Additional Context from Available Data**\n\nFrom the broader insights available in the current directory, I found several relevant AI/development-related news items from the requested timeframe:\n\n1. **Uber's AI Tool Usage Caps (2026-06-03)**\n   - **Product:** General AI coding tools\n   - **Update Type:** Announcement\n   - **Date:** 2026-06-03\n   - **URL:** https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jun/3/uber-caps-usage/\n   - **Description:** Uber implemented usage caps on AI coding tools like Claude Code to manage costs, highlighting economic realities of AI tool adoption at scale\n\n2. **Google's AI Statement Changes (2026-06-04)**\n   - **Product:** Google AI\n   - **Update Type:** Policy\n   - **Date:** 2026-06-04\n   - **URL:** https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jun/4/a-slightly-different-version/\n   - **Description:** Google asked to change their AI statement, removing the phrase about keeping humans in the loop, raising concerns about AI deployment oversight\n\n3. **Anthropic's Security Framework Release (2026-06-04)**\n   - **Product:** Anthropic\n   - **Update Type:** Release\n   - **Date:** 2026-06-04\n   - **URL:** https://github.com/anthropics/defending-code-reference-harness\n   - **Description:** Anthropic released 'defending-code-reference-harness', an open-source framework using AI to discover security vulnerabilities in code\n\n## **Summary**\n\n**Within the requested timeframe (May 23 - June 6, 2026), only Claude Code had significant updates:**\n\n- **7 updates total** for Claude Code\n- **1 major enterprise feature** (v2.1.163 with version management controls)\n- **1 significant security and reliability update** (v2.1.166 with fallback models and hardened messaging)\n- **Multiple incremental improvements** across enterprise features, plugin management, and tool specifications\n\n**Other whitelisted tools (Aider, Continue.dev, Cursor, GitHub Copilot, Windsurf, Devin, Codex CLI, Gemini CLI) had no updates** in this specific timeframe based on the available data.\n\nThe lack of updates from other tools suggests either a slower release cycle during this period, API access limitations, or that these tools may have had updates outside the repositories or channels accessible through the current data sources."
